Right triangle with legs a, b, hypotenuse c by name,
In a square of side a+b, four copies take their frame;
They leave a central square whose side is c the same,
So area is 4·(ab/2) + c²—an equal-measure claim;
Yet also (a+b)² is the area by the very rules of the game,
Set equal, cancel 2ab: c² = a² + b²—Pythagoras in flame.
